# WorkPulse desktop agent — configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    (nothing is mandatory — see below)
#
# The agent loads `.env` from its WORKING DIRECTORY at startup (dotenvy, walking upwards). Real OS
# environment variables take precedence over it. `.env` is gitignored; this example is committed.
#
# ⚠️ A `.env` only reaches the agent when the process starts *in* (or under) the folder holding it —
# true for `just dev` from this repo, NOT true for an installed build launched from the Start menu.
# For an installed agent use real environment variables, or rely on the built-in defaults below.

# ── ALL OPTIONAL — the binary already knows which backend to use ─────────────
# Every value here has a default: baked in at build time by .github/workflows/release.yml, falling
# back to the shared dev stack (src-tauri/src/auth/config.rs). Set one only to point this run
# elsewhere. Resolution order per value: this file / OS env → build-time → dev stack.
#
# That is why a downloaded installer now works with no configuration at all. It did not before:
# `client_id` had no default, the NSIS bundle carries no `.env`, and release.yml injected nothing —
# so every clean install showed "This agent isn't configured for your organization yet" and no
# employee could sign in.
#
# The Cognito App Client ID = the `UserPoolClientId` CDK stack output. Its app client must allow
# USER_PASSWORD_AUTH (docs/RUNBOOK.md); the dev one does.
# WP_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=
# WP_INGEST_URL=https://oqlla6l5oc.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
# WP_COGNITO_REGION=ap-south-1

# ── OPTIONAL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stable per-install agent id (dev override; otherwise a persisted UUID is minted).
# WP_AGENT_ID=

# Updater public key (minisign, from `cargo tauri signer generate`). Unset ⇒ updates disabled.
# WP_UPDATER_PUBKEY=

# Dev conveniences: skip autostart registration and/or the startup update check.
# WP_NO_AUTOSTART=1
# WP_NO_UPDATE=1

# Local agent-state dir (jsonl outbox, agent_id, screenshot temp files).
# WP_STATE_DIR=.agent-state
